 ],
 "notes": "I read lines 1161-1197: 37 stations, one printed line each, no wrapped lines and no second column. 29 have the star for returns and 8 don't (Leman & Ower, Hasbro' L.H., Kentish Knock, Nore, North Foreland, North Sand Head, South Foreland, Casquets).\n\nHow I recorded things:\n- Fragments: I removed only the leading indent. The spacing between the station and keeper columns is kept as printed.\n- Keepers: the list ends every keeper entry with a full stop. I left that stop off the names, but it is still in the fragments. Where two names are joined by '&', I split them into two people. I kept '(mate)' with 'William Rees (mate)' (Newarp L.V.) so the role stays with his name. Remove it if you want bare names.\n- Llyn Wells L.V.: the keeper column says 'The Principal.' This is a job title, not a name, so I put it in 'other' and left keepers empty. Move it if you'd rather keep it on the roll.\n- Longstone has both the star and the dagger, recorded as marks '*†'. The dagger points to the note at line 1158: 'For nature of light, and position and description of station, see report for 1880.' It is the only dagger in the list.\n- Guernsey and Alderney are printed in brackets after the type, e.g. 'Hanois L.H. (Guernsey)'. I gave the place without the brackets.\n- 'No. 5 Buoy, Teesmouth' is the light-vessel's name, not a map number, so I left number empty and kept the whole thing as the name. The list has no map numbers and no light characters.\n- Coast: I used the section heading 'EAST COAST OF ENGLAND' for every row. The Channel Islands lights (Hanois, Casquets) are also listed under it.\n\nKept as printed but worth checking:\n- 'Kentish Knock' has no type printed. It was a light-vessel, but I left type empty.\n- Hasbro' appears twice, as an L.V. (starred) and an L.H. (unstarred). These are two separate stations.\n- Spellings: 'Llyn Wells' (Lynn Well), 'Languard Point' (Landguard), 'Hasbro'' (Happisburgh), 'Orfordness', 'Inner Farne' (written 'Farn, Inner' in other years), 'Spurn (Newsand)', 'Newarp', 'East Side'. Also check these keeper spellings against other years: 'Bonken', 'Perfrement', 'Comben', 'Odgers', 'le Gallais' (lower-case 'le').\n- The prompt repeated the star lead-in in the marks description; the dagger note was the only other mark explanation.",
